# Line endings for GENERATED, TRACKED files - the ones a script rewrites in place.
#
# THE PHANTOM THIS KILLS. Windows checkouts here run with `core.autocrlf=true`, so git writes these
# files to the working tree with CRLF and caches that size in the index. Every generator below
# writes plain "\n". After `npm run build` the bytes are therefore SHORTER than the index expects,
# and git reports the file as modified - while `git diff` shows nothing at all, because the cleaned
# content hashes to the very same blob. Nothing changed; the file just looks changed.
#
# WHAT IT COST. `scripts/merge-order.mjs` and `scripts/safe-merge-preflight.mjs` both refuse to act
# on a dirty worktree, correctly. On 2026-08-21 that phantom marked TWO branches NOT LANDABLE
# (claude/migration-0040-1f501a, claude/template-width-scaling-5dd0a6) over zero changed lines, and
# blocked a safe-merge run mid-flight. A session that runs the build looks unlandable to every tool
# that asks "is this tree clean?".
#
# `text eol=lf` makes checkout write LF, which is what the generators write and what git already
# stores - so the working tree, the index and the generator finally agree. Add a path here when a
# script starts rewriting a tracked file in place; nothing else belongs in this file.
#
# This list is kept honest by `npm run check:line-endings` (in `npm run build`), which fails on any
# file `git status` calls modified that `git diff` cannot see - so a generator nobody declared here
# announces itself the first time it runs, rather than during somebody's landing.

# Rewritten by scripts/build-production-pack.mjs on EVERY `npm run build`.
public/packs/*.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by the catalog sweeps and by `npm run record:e2e-durations`.
e2e/catalog-baseline.json text eol=lf
e2e/catalog-render-baseline.json text eol=lf
scripts/e2e-durations.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by cli/scripts/build-skill.mjs (every `npm --prefix cli run build`; `--check` in the
# root build): the plugin's skill copy, the version-stamped manifests, the package LICENSE.
cli/plugin/skills/** text eol=lf
cli/plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json text eol=lf
cli/plugin/.codex-plugin/plugin.json text eol=lf
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json text eol=lf
cli/LICENSE text eol=lf

# THE REST OF THE GENERATORS, found by auditing every write in `scripts/` against the tracked
# file list on 2026-08-22. These are measurement OUTPUTS - a sweep or a calibration run rewrites
# the file in place and the numbers are then committed as the baseline - so each one is a tree
# that goes phantom-dirty the moment somebody runs the sweep, which is mid-session, which is when
# `merge-order` and `safe-merge-preflight` are asked whether the tree is clean.
benchmarks/pro/v1/spike/*-calibration.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/pro/v1/spike/occlusion-sweep.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/pro/v1/spike/mark-clearance-sweep.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/pro/v1/spike/structure-margins.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/pro/evidence/plate-legibility.json text eol=lf
# The default --report target of scripts/design-rules-audit-sweep.mjs.
benchmarks/design-rules/AUDIT-*.md text eol=lf
benchmarks/video/model-catalog.json text eol=lf
supabase/advisor-baseline.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by `npm run check:copy -- --update` (scripts/check-copy.mjs): the per-file
# baseline of copy tells that predate the gate.
scripts/copy-baseline.json text eol=lf

# Rewritten by scripts/behaviour-docs.mjs (`npm run write:behaviour-docs`; `--check` in the root
# build), which regenerates the §5b naming tables from src/templates/behaviours/words.json.
docs/SVG_AUTHORING.md text eol=lf
# The rule store and what it compiles to: rewritten in place by scripts/compile-contracts.mjs and
# scripts/learn.mjs with LF, so an autocrlf checkout must not report them phantom-dirty.
contracts/**/*.md text eol=lf
.claude/rules/*.md text eol=lf

# MERGING A GENERATED CONTRACT IS MEANINGLESS, so it is not attempted. Every file below is
# rendered from contracts/rules/, and when two branches each record a rule the correct content is
# the rendering of the MERGED store - which neither side contains. `merge=noacg-contracts`
# (scripts/contracts-merge-driver.mjs, registered by `npm run contracts:compile`) regenerates
# instead, and `check:contracts` in the build is what proves the result is current.
#
# A MIGRATED AREA CARRIES ITS OWN LINE, in its own directory's .gitattributes, written by the
# compiler. That is deliberate: two areas migrating at once then edit two different files rather
# than both editing this one, which is the conflict phase 2b exists to remove.
.claude/rules/*.md merge=noacg-contracts
contracts/index.md merge=noacg-contracts
